# Fixbyte Templates: project context

- Preserve the static *output*: what ships is plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. Build-time Python scripts in `scripts/` are fine. Do not introduce a framework, bundler, package manager, or server-side runtime unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Primary pages are static HTML templates; shared styling belongs in `css/style.css`, client-side behavior in `js/`, and editable content in `data/*.json` when the existing data model supports it.
- Keep changes focused, backwards-compatible, and minimal. Do not rewrite unrelated code.
- Do not add analytics, tracking, external scripts, CDNs, or remote dependencies without explicit approval.
- Treat `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `.cursor/agents/` as project guidance. Use the relevant marketing agent files when changing positioning, landing-page copy, CTAs, or growth assets.
